{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8362727ed810bdf9","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9014-E001\n3\ttitle: GA-readiness assessment for Llama Stack\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9014\n5\tcomponent: Llama Stack\n6\tteam: RHOAI GenAI\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tinvestigation_signals:\n11\t  question_specificity: 1\n12\t  source_accessibility: 1\n13\t  local_runnability: 1\n14\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -1\n15\t  human_judgment_required: -1\n16\timplementation_type: null\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Medium\n19\tai_implementability_score: 1\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# GA-readiness assessment for Llama Stack\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tResolve the strategy's central unknown: no systematic GA-readiness assessment\n30\tof Llama Stack has been done, and TP feedback is scattered across support\n31\ttickets. This epic inventories the gaps between current Tech Preview quality\n32\tand the GA bar — across API stability, upgrade paths, scale limits, and error\n33\thandling — and produces the definitive GA scope. The outcome determines the\n34\tsize and content of the downstream stability, hardening, and support-posture\n35\twork.\n36\t\n37\t## Scope\n38\t\n39\t- Systematic assessment of the Llama Stack distribution (operator, CRD,\n40\t  distribution defaults, published API surface) against the GA bar in four\n41\t  areas: API stability, upgrade paths, scale limits, and error handling.\n42\t- Triage of Tech Preview feedback from support tickets into concrete,\n43\t  evidenced gap items.\n44\t- Severity and GA-impact scoring for every identified gap.\n45\t- A definitive GA scope document that maps each gap to a disposition\n46\t  (fix for GA / defer / accept risk) and identifies the downstream\n47\t  remediation work it implies.\n48\t- Cross-check of the assessment's architecture premises (CRD surface,\n49\t  deployment model, provider integrations, maturity state) against the\n50\t  platform's architecture context.\n51\t\n52\t## Acceptance Criteria\n53\t\n54\t- A gap inventory exists that covers all four assessed areas (API stability,\n55\t  upgrade paths, scale limits, error handling), with every gap carrying a\n56\t  severity, supporting evidence, and a GA-impact statement.\n57\t- Tech Preview feedback from support tickets is triaged and reflected as gap\n58\t  items (or explicitly recorded as not GA-relevant).\n59\t- A definitive GA scope document is produced in which every inventory item\n60\t  has a disposition and a mapping to downstream remediation work.\n61\t- The dispositions are reviewed with product and support stakeholders and\n62\t  the review outcome is recorded in the scope document.\n63\t\n64\t## HLR Traceability\n65\t\n66\t- HLR-1 (P0): full coverage — this epic is the GA-readiness assessment that\n67\t  inventories the gaps and produces the definitive GA scope.\n68\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8c6d160a01e76188","agent_id":"a5f8ac71d1d2d3442","session_id":"85972203-1fc3-4cec-8474-9537ba830cbb","uuid":"5125f2e1-910e-4667-8b66-024f87bc35c3","timestamp":"2026-10-26T11:27:59.176Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8362727ed810bdf9","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-9014 decomposition"}
