nt's architecture premises (CRD surface,\n49\t  deployment model, provider integrations, maturity state) against the\n50\t  platform's architecture context.\n51\t\n52\t## Acceptance Criteria\n53\t\n54\t- A gap inventory exists that covers all four assessed areas (API stability,\n55\t  upgrade paths, scale limits, error handling), with every gap carrying a\n56\t  severity, supporting evidence, and a GA-impact statement.\n57\t- Tech Preview feedback from support tickets is triaged and reflected as gap\n58\t  items (or explicitly recorded as not GA-relevant).\n59\t- A definitive GA scope document is produced in which every inventory item\n60\t  has a disposition and a mapping to downstream remediation work.\n61\t- The dispositions are reviewed with product and support stakeholders and\n62\t  the review outcome is recorded in the scope document.\n63\t\n64\t## HLR Traceability\n65\t\n66\t- HLR-1 (P0): full coverage — this epic is the GA-readiness assessment that\n67\t  inventories the gaps and produces the definitive GA scope.\n68\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8f45671fc647b77e","agent_id":"a6524b9534eb44486","session_id":"85972203-1fc3-4cec-8474-9537ba830cbb","uuid":"0497ac3a-58b8-439b-954a-7f6f880adf4a","timestamp":"2026-10-26T11:30:05.066Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-80f3ffbae6402cc8","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9014 decomposition"}
